ally  firstly there was the way that he stared  out at you that was worrying if you  added that to the way that he would read  out to you then it was the sort of thing  that could easily give a child  nightmares Furby some toys become  genuine pop culture phenomenon one great  example of this was the Furby if you  were a kid back in the 1990's we think  that you would have had one of these  they were like an animatronic pet you  had to look after it and it would talk  to you looking back on it it was a  pretty big surprise that we weren't more  creeped out by our fur bees think about  it they looked a bit odd and they talked  a lot there were even reports that they  used to turn themselves back on even  after they were sweet  stuff like we said spooky struts we  think that it's fair to say that my  little pony was and is a genuine  pop-culture phenomenon the toys have  inspired several generations of games TV  shows and even movies but when something  becomes popular it's not uncommon that  things inspired by it follow the lead  that's what happened with struts which  were like My Little Pony except a bit  more creepy they aren't as cartoony so  they have the unintentional result of  looking a bit like the sort of big horse  that would pick on the Little Ponies at  school we can't quite put our fingers on  it but they definitely creep us out  Cyclops brain baby stroller when a baby  gets a little bit older it will often  end up being taken out in a baby  stroller  they are usually fairly nice and  everyday things that is why we felt a  little bit icky by this thing that's  supposed to be a device for babies it's  a baby stroller but it doesn't look like  what what it looks like is a brain but  not just any sort of brain if you look  around the front it's a head but the  head only has one eye so it's a cyclops  brain baby stroller we don't know if  it's completely horrible or secretly  pretty cool Mexican jumping beans kids  quite often like toys that are a bit  unus